<h2>Two different mango trades under one HS code</h2>
<p>This is worth understanding before requesting a quote, because it explains a pricing pattern that otherwise looks confusing. The trade data shows a striking split in unit value by destination: the United States imports at roughly USD 2.88 per kg, while Saudi Arabia imports at about USD 0.90 per kg — more than three times the difference. That's not the same mango priced differently by market; it reflects two genuinely different trades. Western markets (US, UK, Germany) receive air-freighted, premium-variety fruit — Alphonso and Kesar above all — sold into specialty and high-end retail channels. Gulf markets receive a higher-volume mix, often sea-freighted, at correspondingly lower prices.</p>

<h2>Where UK trade sits</h2>
<p>The UK imported roughly USD 16.9 million under this HS category (which also includes guava and mangosteen, though mango dominates the value) in calendar 2024 — squarely in the premium-market tier alongside the US and Germany, reflecting the UK's established Alphonso demand, driven substantially by South Asian diaspora communities and increasingly by broader specialty-food retail interest.</p>

<h2>Air freight is the default for this trade</h2>
<p>Premium mango to the UK moves predominantly by air, not sea. Alphonso in particular has a short shelf life once ripe, and air freight preserves the quality and freshness that justifies the retail premium buyers pay. This is a fundamentally different logistics conversation from our sea-freight fresh fruit lines like grapes or pomegranate — shorter transit, but a different cost structure entirely.</p>

<h2>Season: a hard constraint, not a soft one</h2>
<p>Alphonso mango is available roughly March through June, typically peaking April-May. There is no meaningful off-season supply for fresh fruit — this isn't a product where "we can source it anytime with enough notice" applies. If you're planning a UK mango programme, build your buying calendar around this window, and check our <a href="/resources/harvest-calendar/">harvest calendar</a> for the broader seasonal picture across our product range.</p>

<h2>Specification for a UK order</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Variety</strong> — Alphonso, Kesar or other, each with distinct flavour and market positioning</li>
  <li><strong>Size/count grading</strong> — matched to your retail or food-service format</li>
  <li><strong>Ripeness at dispatch</strong> — calibrated to your specific air-freight transit time</li>
  <li><strong>Pesticide residue testing</strong> — given strict UK/EU limits, strongly recommended pre-shipment</li>
</ul>
